  "faqs": [
    { "q": "Is this a medical diagnosis tool?", "a": "No. Whole Care coordinates your case — intake, hospital matching, quotations and logistics. All diagnosis and treatment decisions are made by licensed doctors at the treating hospital." },
    { "q": "How is my cost estimate calculated?", "a": "The calculator uses sourced specialty price ranges for the procedure and destination, plus typical stay length and travel costs. Hospitals then confirm a binding quotation for your specific case." },
    { "q": "What does the AI actually do?", "a": "It organizes your submitted case into a structured summary for care coordinators, and helps you prepare questions before a doctor consultation. It never diagnoses or recommends treatment." },
    { "q": "How are hospitals verified?", "a": "Each listed hospital carries a recognized accreditation (JCI or NABH) and a last-verified date. The MVP directory covers a seeded set of partner hospitals; the model scales by onboarding accredited partners with signed agreements." },
    { "q": "Is my data secure?", "a": "Case data is tied to your account and only visible to you and the hospitals you explicitly send your case to. This MVP uses a simple file-backed store suited for a pilot; production deployments move to an encrypted database." }
